xcb: use a byte buffer for XInput 2 event masks (big-endian)

Backport to Qt 5.15.18 of qtbase commit a875503d9e001a05eb3c0998f6c1292f0fefc4e1
"xcb: Use byte buffer for event masks" (Povilas Kanapickas, 2021-09-28,
https://github.com/qt/qtbase/commit/a875503d9e001a05eb3c0998f6c1292f0fefc4e1),
which is in Qt 6 only. From its message: "since the XI protocol always sends
the masks using little-endian, the XI protocol support on big-endian machines
was currently broken."

On big-endian hosts (SPARC) Qt 5.15 stores the XI2 event mask as a uint32_t
number, so its bytes reach the X server reversed: XI_ButtonPress (bit 4)
arrives as bit 28 (XI_GesturePinchUpdate). Xorg 21.1 rejects such a partial
gesture selection with BadValue, so Qt windows receive no XI2 events: no
mouse wheel scrolling, no XI2 grab for popup menus. Little-endian hosts
produce the same bytes as before.

Upstream hunks 1-3 apply as they are. Qt 5.15 has two more places that
build masks as numbers, absent from Qt 6, converted the same way:
xi2SelectDeviceEventsCompatibility() (touch, tablet and scrolling devices)
and xi2SetMouseGrabEnabled() (upstream's hunk 4, on the 5.15 code).

Upstream: not in Qt 5.15 open source nor KDE's kde/5.15 (checked
2026-11-23); a candidate for KDE's Qt 5.15 patch collection.

--- qt-everywhere-src-5.15.18/qtbase/src/plugins/platforms/xcb/qxcbconnection_xi2.cpp.orig
